# What this repo takes from ContainerHub. One row per asset: the id from
# third_party/ContainerHub/shared/config/shared-assets.manifest, and a path only
# when the copy does not sit at that registry row's default.
#
# Checked by:
#   bash third_party/ContainerHub/shared/config/sync-shared-config.sh --repo-root . --check
#
# None of the five shared configs is taken: this is a Rust crate, with no
# CMakeLists.txt and no C++ for the clang tools, cmake-format or gcovr to read.
# Only the two bootstrap templates are shared here - the two files that cannot
# be consumed by reference, because each one is what FINDS ContainerHub.

containerhub-sh
resolve-build-module
